        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(write): add append mode to prevent silent data loss",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `write` tool always overwrites files completely. When multiple isolated sessions (e.g., main session + cron jobs) write to the same shared file, the last write wins and **prior content is silently destroyed** with no warning, no backup, and no recovery path. This is especially dangerous with cron/isolated sessions, where sub-agents independently decide to \"log results\" to a shared file and overwrite hours of main-session work.\n\nPrompt-level guards are insufficient — sub-agents ignore or forget \"NEVER overwrite\" / \"APPEND ONLY\" instructions under complex task prompts.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe existing `write` tool provides no append primitive. To append, an agent must:\n1. Read the full file\n2. Concatenate new content\n3. Write the entire result back\n\nThis is wasteful, error-prone, and most models naturally interpret \"write\" as \"append\" rather than \"overwrite.\" Adding a first-class `append: true` parameter resolves the root cause — agents can append without synthesizing a read-concatenate-overwrite sequence.\n\nInternal primitives already exist: `fs.appendFile` for host paths, `root.append()` for workspace-scoped paths in `@openclaw/fs-safe`. This change exposes them through the model-facing tool API.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- **No breaking change**: default behavior (no `append` param) is identical — overwrite\n- **New capability**: `write` with `append: true` appends instead of overwrites\n- **Safer default**: append mode skips the \"identical content → no-op\" optimization so intentional duplicate content is preserved\n- **Backward-compatible**: existing write operations, prompts, and workflows unchanged\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Unit tests (12/12 passing)\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  12 passed (12)\n```\n\n5 new tests covering:\n- Append to existing file preserves prior content\n- Append to non-existent path creates the file\n- Default overwrite still works when append is not set\n- Overwrite with identical content still returns no-op\n- Malformed `append: \"true\"` (string) is rejected with clear error\n\n### Live proof\n\n```\nStep 1 - Write initial (overwrite):    content=\"line 1\\n\"                    ✅\nStep 2 - Append to existing file:      content=\"line 1\\nline 2\\n\"            ✅\nStep 3 - Overwrite (default):          content=\"replaced\\n\"                  ✅\nStep 4 - Append to new file (creates): content=\"fresh\\n\"                     ✅\nStep 5 - Overwrite identical content:  \"No changes made ...\"                 ✅\n```\n\n### Scope\n\n**4 files changed**, 0 unrelated changes:\n- `src/agents/sessions/tools/write.ts` — core schema/execute/recovery\n- `src/agents/sessions/tools/tool-contracts.ts` — WriteToolInput type\n- `src/agents/agent-tools.read.ts` — appendFile for sandbox/host/workspace paths\n- `src/agents/sessions/tools/write.test.ts` — 5 new append-mode tests\n\nCloses #40001",
        "branch": "fix/write-append-mode",
